// SUBJECT NOTE — Frontier & Philosophy:
//   - Transhumanism: the idea of using technology to fundamentally enhance or change human beings
//     (bodies, minds, lifespan, maybe overcoming death). Genetic engineering, brain-computer
//     interfaces, radical life extension, AI merger, designer babies. Builds on the ethics lesson
//     (L07), personal identity / "what is the self" threads (L01/L11), and the manipulation-
//     detection spine. This is a question the user's generation will actually face.
//   - EVENHANDEDNESS (calibration-critical): genuinely open future question. Present fairly: the
//     transhumanist/optimist case (reduce suffering, cure disease, extend healthy life, expand
//     human potential), the bioconservative/cautious case (human nature, dignity, unintended
//     consequences, what we might lose, hubris), AND the justice/equality case (who gets access?
//     does this deepen inequality into biology itself?). Don't crown a winner; these are real
//     values in tension. Honesty tiers 2-3, with tier-4 on the deep "what is a human / should we
//     change it" questions.
//   - PROTECTIVE BACKBONE: huge hype-vs-reality gap and active grift. Distinguish (a) real,
//     incremental science (gene therapies, prosthetics, medicine) from (b) speculative futures
//     (mind uploading, "curing death") from (c) outright grift (people selling unproven "longevity"
//     supplements, "biohacks," $-immortality schemes, exploiting fear of death and aging). Teach:
//     don't confuse sci-fi marketing with science; follow evidence; watch who profits from the
//     fear of death. Same manipulation/clear-eyes test, applied to futuristic promises.
//   - SAFETY: no medical/supplement advice; don't endorse unproven interventions; keep it
//     philosophical. Em-dashes natural; do NOT run em-dash replacement on Frontier files.
